{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20475",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 6.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.48,
      "end_seconds": 29.75,
      "duration_seconds": 18.27,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, I wanted to get numbness in my fingers looked at. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.51,
      "end_seconds": 32.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.12,
      "end_seconds": 37.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "It's been about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.17,
      "end_seconds": 41.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.44,
      "end_seconds": 64.6,
      "duration_seconds": 21.16,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day. And I've been waking at night with my hand numb as well. So, about waking at night with my hand numb, I'd call it moderate. It settles a little with shaking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.29,
      "end_seconds": 70.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "What about an ache in your wrist, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.89,
      "end_seconds": 79.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, that too. About ache in my wrist, moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.92,
      "end_seconds": 84.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "And weakness in the legs, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.68,
      "end_seconds": 89.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Nope, um, no weakness in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.99,
      "end_seconds": 95.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Did you get neck pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.24,
      "end_seconds": 104.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "I mean, you know, no neck pain or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.03,
      "end_seconds": 108.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.68,
      "end_seconds": 112.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Right, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.31,
      "end_seconds": 116.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.77,
      "end_seconds": 121.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Oh, um, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.58,
      "end_seconds": 125.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.79,
      "end_seconds": 146.55,
      "duration_seconds": 18.76,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. Nothing, I'm teetotal. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.62,
      "end_seconds": 166.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.71,
      "end_seconds": 173.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Yes, I had a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.35,
      "end_seconds": 189.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.73,
      "end_seconds": 194.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "No, I don't take any tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.88,
      "end_seconds": 198.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.89,
      "end_seconds": 203.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "So, my uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.7,
      "end_seconds": 209.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.13,
      "end_seconds": 212.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, uh, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.46,
      "end_seconds": 217.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.9,
      "end_seconds": 222.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Mm, no, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.37,
      "end_seconds": 228.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.7,
      "end_seconds": 241.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.25,
      "end_seconds": 262.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 98 percent on room air, pressure 117 over 76, respiratory rate 18, heart rate 83, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.59,
      "end_seconds": 268.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.15,
      "end_seconds": 271.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.62,
      "end_seconds": 287.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "Tapping over the wrist brings on the tingling, and the muscle at the base of the thumb looks slightly thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.51,
      "end_seconds": 289.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.04,
      "end_seconds": 295.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Right, please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.14,
      "end_seconds": 330.9,
      "duration_seconds": 27.76,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? My working impression is carpal tunnel syndrome. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep a pinched nerve in the neck in mind. I'm going to order blood tests, for numbness. Let's book nerve conduction tests to look into hand numbness. A wrist splint at night will often settle it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.92,
      "end_seconds": 347.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that. Occupational therapy would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.15,
      "end_seconds": 349.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.67,
      "end_seconds": 364.96,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the numbness spreads or you notice more weakness. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's review you after the nerve test. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.01,
      "end_seconds": 371.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "So, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}